# Line-ending policy for cross-platform (Windows + Linux) development.
#
# Why this file exists: with `core.autocrlf=true` (Git for Windows' default),
# a Windows checkout rewrites LF -> CRLF in text files. POSIX shell scripts then
# fail when executed by /bin/sh (dash) inside the Linux API/Celery containers:
#   apps/api/scripts/entrypoint.sh: 14: set: Illegal option -
# which crash-loops every container that runs entrypoint.sh. These rules make
# each file's line endings a property of the REPO, independent of any developer's
# personal `core.autocrlf` setting — so the bug cannot recur on a fresh clone.

# Default: treat files as text, auto-detect, and store LF in the repository.
* text=auto

# --- Must be LF everywhere (run by /bin/sh or bash inside Linux containers/CI) ---
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile    text eol=lf
docker-compose*.yml text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.env           text eol=lf
.env.*          text eol=lf
Makefile        text eol=lf
*.mk            text eol=lf

# --- Must stay CRLF (Windows-native scripts) ---
*.ps1           text eol=crlf
*.bat           text eol=crlf
*.cmd           text eol=crlf

# --- Binary: never apply line-ending or diff conversion ---
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
*.eot  binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
